# SEO-NextJS.mdc Rules

## Metadata & Head Configuration

- [ ] **Page Title**
  - Descriptive, keyword-rich title under 60 characters
  - Unique for each page
  - Format: `Primary Keyword | Brand Name`

- [ ] **Meta Description**
  - Compelling description under 155-160 characters
  - Contains target keywords naturally
  - Describes page content accurately
  - Includes call-to-action when appropriate

- [ ] **Meta Tags**
  - Implement proper robots meta tag
  - Include proper viewport settings
  - Set correct charset
  - Include canonical URL meta tag to prevent duplicate content issues

- [ ] **Open Graph & Twitter Cards**
  - OG title matches page title
  - OG description provides preview text
  - OG image (1200×630px) exists for social sharing
  - OG type, locale, and URL are properly set
  - Twitter card type and appropriate fields set

## JSON-LD Structured Data

- [ ] **Base Schema Implementation**
  - Include appropriate schema type based on content (Article, Product, FAQ, etc.)
  - Validate structured data using Google's Rich Results Test
  - Implement using standard JSON-LD format

- [ ] **Schema Completeness**
  - All required properties for each schema type added
  - Include recommended properties for richer search results
  - Date fields use ISO 8601 format
  - Author and publisher information included where applicable

- [ ] **Organization/Local Business Schema**
  - Add Organization schema to homepage
  - Include logo, contact info, social profiles
  - Add location data for local businesses

## Performance Optimization

- [ ] **Core Web Vitals**
  - LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) < 2.5s
  - FID (First Input Delay) < 100ms
  - CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift) < 0.1
  - INP (Interaction to Next Paint) < 200ms

- [ ] **Image Optimization**
  - Use Next.js Image component for all images
  - Set explicit width and height to prevent layout shifts
  - Add descriptive alt text for all images
  - Add priority attribute for LCP images
  - Use responsive images with appropriate sizes

- [ ] **Font Optimization**
  - Use next/font to optimize font loading
  - Implement font-display strategy
  - Subset fonts when possible
  - Minimize font variations

- [ ] **JavaScript Optimization**
  - Minimize unused JavaScript
  - Use dynamic imports for non-critical components
  - Implement code splitting where appropriate
  - Use lightweight alternatives when possible

## Rendering Strategy

- [ ] **Page Rendering Method**
  - Use SSG for static content pages
  - Use SSR for dynamic, personalized content
  - Use ISR for semi-dynamic content
  - Implement proper data fetching methods (getStaticProps, getServerSideProps)

- [ ] **Hydration Strategy**
  - Minimize client-side JavaScript for faster hydration
  - Use React.lazy and Suspense for client components
  - Implement streaming SSR where appropriate
  - Test hydration errors and performance

## URL Structure & Navigation

- [ ] **URL Optimization**
  - Create clean, descriptive URLs (no IDs or parameters when possible)
  - Include target keywords in URLs
  - Use hyphens to separate words
  - Keep URLs concise and logical

- [ ] **Navigation Structure**
  - Implement breadcrumbs with structured data
  - Ensure logical site hierarchy
  - Limit navigation depth (max 3 clicks from homepage)
  - Include XML sitemap linked from robots.txt

- [ ] **Internal Linking**
  - Link related pages with descriptive anchor text
  - Add relevant internal links in content
  - Implement a flat site architecture
  - Link to important pages from homepage

## Mobile Optimization

- [ ] **Responsive Design**
  - Test on multiple devices and screen sizes
  - Ensure tap targets are properly sized (min 48×48px)
  - Implement proper viewport settings
  - Test with Chrome DevTools mobile emulation

- [ ] **Mobile Performance**
  - Ensure mobile page speed score >90
  - Optimize for mobile-first indexing
  - Test scrolling performance
  - Remove intrusive interstitials

## Content Quality

- [ ] **Content Structure**
  - Use proper heading hierarchy (H1, H2, H3)
  - Include target keyword in H1
  - Keep content organized with subheadings
  - Use short paragraphs and bulleted lists when appropriate

- [ ] **Content Depth**
  - Create comprehensive content that answers user intent
  - Ensure appropriate content length based on topic
  - Include relevant LSI keywords
  - Use multimedia (images, videos) to enhance content

## Technical SEO

- [ ] **Sitemap**
  - Generate XML sitemap with next-sitemap
  - Include all important pages
  - Exclude low-value pages
  - Submit to Google Search Console

- [ ] **Robots.txt**
  - Create proper robots.txt file
  - Block unimportant directories
  - Allow important directories
  - Link to sitemap

- [ ] **Canonical Tags**
  - Implement canonical tags for all pages
  - Handle pagination with rel="next" and rel="prev"
  - Properly handle multi-language content with hreflang

- [ ] **Status Codes**
  - Return proper HTTP status codes (200, 301, 404, etc.)
  - Implement custom 404 page
  - Set up 301 redirects for changed URLs
  - Monitor and fix 404 errors

## Analytics & Monitoring

- [ ] **Analytics Setup**
  - Implement Google Analytics or alternative
  - Set up conversion tracking
  - Configure enhanced ecommerce (if applicable)
  - Create custom events for important interactions

- [ ] **Search Console**
  - Verify property in Google Search Console
  - Submit sitemap
  - Monitor and fix crawl errors
  - Check for manual actions

- [ ] **Monitoring Tools**
  - Set up automated monitoring for broken links
  - Monitor core web vitals
  - Set up alerts for traffic drops
  - Track keyword rankings

## Next.js Specific Optimizations

- [ ] **Script Optimization**
  - Use Next.js Script component with proper strategy
  - Implement proper script loading priorities
  - Load third-party scripts appropriately
  - Minimize render-blocking scripts

- [ ] **Route Optimization**
  - Implement dynamic routes efficiently
  - Preload critical routes
  - Use shallow routing where appropriate
  - Implement prefetching for likely navigations

- [ ] **API Routes**
  - Implement API caching
  - Optimize API response times
  - Secure API endpoints
  - Handle errors gracefully

- [ ] **Next-SEO Implementation**
  - Consider using next-seo package
  - Set default SEO settings in _app.js
  - Override SEO settings on a page-by-page basis
  - Implement required JSON-LD components

## Advanced SEO

- [ ] **Internationalization**
  - Implement hreflang tags for language variations
  - Use proper URL structure for multilingual content
  - Configure language detection
  - Create language switcher

- [ ] **Schema Expansion**
  - Implement BreadcrumbList schema
  - Add FAQ schema for question-based content
  - Implement HowTo schema for instructional content
  - Use appropriate schema for video content

- [ ] **Progressive Web App**
  - Implement service workers
  - Create app manifest
  - Enable offline functionality
  - Implement push notifications

- [ ] **E-commerce Optimizations**
  - Add product schema with reviews
  - Implement proper faceted navigation
  - Handle out-of-stock products appropriately
  - Optimize category pages

## Security

- [ ] **HTTPS Implementation**
  - Ensure all pages use HTTPS
  - Implement proper SSL certificate
  - Set up HSTS headers
  - Redirect HTTP to HTTPS

- [ ] **Content Security**
  - Implement CSP headers
  - Set up XSS protection
  - Prevent clickjacking
  - Secure cookies and localStorage

## Testing & Validation

- [ ] **SEO Validation**
  - Test with Lighthouse
  - Validate structured data
  - Check mobile friendliness
  - Verify indexability

- [ ] **Accessibility**
  - Meet WCAG 2.1 AA standards
  - Implement proper ARIA attributes
  - Ensure keyboard navigation
  - Provide alternative text for non-text elements

## Deployment

- [ ] **CDN Configuration**
  - Deploy on a CDN (Vercel, Netlify, etc.)
  - Enable edge caching
  - Configure cache headers
  - Implement image CDN if needed

- [ ] **CI/CD**
  - Include SEO checks in CI pipeline
  - Test SEO metrics before deployment
  - Monitor post-deployment performance
  - Implement canary deployments